.Dd June 26, 2026
.Dt CAP_XFER_CAPMODE 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cap_xfer_capmode
.Nd restrict descriptor transfer to capability-mode receivers
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/capsicum.h
.Ft int
.Fn cap_xfer_capmode "int fd"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn cap_xfer_capmode
system call sets a monotonic per-descriptor flag that restricts who may
receive the descriptor when it is passed via
.Xr recvmsg 2
with an
.Dv SCM_RIGHTS
control message or via mac_capability message passing.
Once set, the flag requires that the receiving process already be in
capability mode
.Pq see Xr cap_enter 2 .
If the receiver is not in capability mode,
.Xr recvmsg 2
fails with
.Er ENOTCAPABLE
and the descriptor is not delivered.
.Pp
The flag is monotonic: once set it cannot be cleared.
Calling
.Fn cap_xfer_capmode
on a descriptor that already has the flag set is permitted and has no
effect.
.Pp
This system call controls
.Em who
may receive the descriptor.
It is orthogonal to
.Xr cap_xfer_limit 2 ,
which controls
.Em how many times
the descriptor may be transferred, and may be combined with it freely.
.Pp
.Sy Flag propagation:
when a capability-mode process successfully receives the descriptor, the
new descriptor installed in the receiver's file descriptor table inherits
the flag.
Subsequent transfers of the received descriptor are therefore also
restricted to capability-mode receivers.
The flag cannot be cleared by the receiving process.
.Pp
This system call is allowed in capability mode
.Pq see Xr cap_enter 2 .
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
Combined with
.Xr cap_xfer_limit 2
.Pq Dv CAP_XFER_ONCE ,
.Xr cap_cloexec_limit 2
.Pq Dv CAP_CLOEXEC_LOCKED ,
.Xr cap_clofork_limit 2
.Pq Dv CAP_CLOFORK_LOCKED ,
and
.Xr cap_ambient_limit 2 ,
.Fn cap_xfer_capmode
creates a closed security boundary: the descriptor can be received
exactly once, only by a sandboxed process already in capability mode,
will be closed on exec or fork in that sandboxed process, and cannot
escape through ambient authority checks.
This pattern is appropriate when delegating a sensitive resource to a
sandboxed worker that must not be able to exfiltrate it further.
.Pp
A complementary mechanism,
.Dv LOCAL_CAPMODE_CONNECT
.Pq see Xr unix 4 ,
enforces capability-mode requirements at connection time rather than
at descriptor transfer time.
When set on a listening
.Ux Ns -domain
socket, only processes in capability mode may connect to it.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Rv -std
.Sh ERRORS
.Fn cap_xfer_capmode
succeeds unless:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EBADF
The
.Fa fd
argument is not a valid active descriptor.
.It Bq Er ENOSYS
The running kernel was compiled without
.Cd "options CAPABILITIES" .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cap_ambient_limit 2 ,
.Xr cap_clofork_limit 2 ,
.Xr cap_cloexec_limit 2 ,
.Xr cap_enter 2 ,
.Xr cap_rights_limit 2 ,
.Xr cap_xfer_limit 2 ,
.Xr recvmsg 2 ,
.Xr capsicum 4 ,
.Xr unix 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn cap_xfer_capmode
system call first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
